Here are the final frontend file updates and the exact backend routes needed in server.js to make the new interactive courses work:

1. Frontend File Updates:

Deleted: learning-path.html (Replaced by modules).

Added: courses.html (The Course Catalog page).

Added: course-modules.html (The specific course page with chapters, slides, and quizzes).

Kept: quiz.html (The interactive quiz engine).

2. Required Backend Routes:

GET /courses: Fetch all courses from the database and render courses.html. Pass all_courses, is_logged_in, and cart_count to the template.

GET /modules/:courseId: Fetch the specific course and an array of its chapters. Ensure chapters include slides_url and the logged-in user's progress (0-100). Render course-modules.html.

GET /quiz/:chapterId: Fetch quiz questions for that chapter, convert them to a JSON string (JSON.stringify), and pass it to quiz.html as a variable named questions_json.

POST /api/quiz/submit: Catch the submitted form (chapter_id and score), save the score to the database to update the user's progress, and redirect them back to the modules page.

